// Pattern variables a closure captures are declared like any other local: each
// iteration's `Unpack r4, r1, 2` writes the new values straight into the
// registers of `a` and `b`, replacing the cells the previous iteration's
// closure captured.
// compile: stdlib
fn f(xs: [(Int, Int)]) { for (a, b) in xs { fn() { a + b }; } }
